"A1 iteration 6 is done: one general engine change, engine `e3-1.8.0`. Bends folded the wrong way are now found, measured and published. Per-bend correctness given CAD is now 0.901.\n\n**Start state.** This was the second start of iteration 6. The first start took the snapshot (`engine_before.tgz`, sha `e3479492\u2026`) and ran only diagnostics, so the engine still matched it byte for byte and I kept it. Iteration 5 had not regressed and its generality check was clean, so nothing was reverted or removed.\n\n**The change** (in `inspect/articulated.py`, `metrology.py`, `engine.py`, `config.py`):\n- **Mirrored hinge search.** A child folded to the other side of its parent's plane is searched for about the CAD axis reflected across the parent's mid-plane. Before, the engine read clutter there and reported UNKNOWN.\n- **Guards.** The reading only replaces the normal one if:\n  - it uses material no fitted panel owns;\n  - it shows a second parallel skin 0.4\u20131.6 sheet thicknesses away (a thin lip's skins read only about 0.6 mm apart on a 0.935 mm sheet);\n  - its support is at least 1.5\u00d7 the normal reading's.\n- **Chosen pose only.** The search runs after the pose is picked, so pose choices are exactly iteration 5's. Running it on every candidate pose could let an upside-down pose read every bend as reversed and win, so I dropped that version.\n- **Bend line by mirror symmetry.** The angle FAILs (as in iteration 5's fix C). The line is published at the fold's own outer sharp, and its position is measured on that sharp reflected back across the parent's mid-plane. Flange lengths stay UNKNOWN.\n- **Two new config fields:** `reversed_support_ratio` 1.5 and `reversed_two_skin_share` 0.2, both range-checked. No frozen threshold changed and there is no part-specific logic.\n\n**Results.** Only one of the 26 runnable physical cases changed: 23553000 SCAN_2, where hooks B2 and B14 now read about 119\u00b0 the wrong way. Both angles FAIL (299\u00b0 against 60\u00b0), positions read +1.11 mm (FAIL) and +0.59 mm (REVIEW), and both lines are published.\n\n| Measure | Iteration 5 | Iteration 6 | Best F1 lane, same scans |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| BROAD, frozen gold: recall | 0.729 | 0.743 | 0.451 |\n| BROAD, frozen gold: micro F1 | 0.693 | 0.702 | 0.508 |\n| BROAD, frozen gold: family-macro F1 | 0.814 | 0.817 | 0.543 |\n| BROAD scans, gold of record: precision / recall | 0.987 / 0.981 | 0.988 / 0.994 | 0.679 / 0.475 |\n| Per-bend correctness given CAD (riser-aware) | 181/203 (0.892) | 183/203 (0.901) | \u2014 |\n\n- The two hooks count only under the riser-aware definition. Strict per-bend correctness stays 170/203, and the same 3 false-PASS proxies remain.\n- GOLD_SET_V1 (0.990 micro / 0.974 family-macro) and the Gold11 relabel (0.987) are unchanged.\n- **G2 and G3:** same verdicts as iteration 5. The only change is G3 formed-bend angle coverage, 77/81 \u2192 79/81.\n- **Regression checks:**\n  - The 50-case synthetic regression tier passes with every accuracy gate identical to iteration 5.\n  - All 113 CAD-stage probes give identical values to iteration 5.\n  - The new search triggered nowhere except the two hooks.\n  - The 150 engine tests pass, 8 of them new.\n- **Synthetic wrong-way probes** on 9 recipes, same scans run through both engines:\n  - Bends folded fully the wrong way read their true angle within about 0.1\u00b0.\n  - Positions read within 0.04 mm, except one rolled part at \u22120.87 mm.\n  - Iteration 5's engine read these bends as UNKNOWN, wrong values, or \"not yet formed\".\n- **Runtime:** one extra fit per scan; 95th-percentile physical runtime is 27.9 s (was 26.9 s).\n\n**Not changed:**\n- **The 2 tab lines on 38172000 SCAN_1** are a question for the owner, not an engine fix.\n  - The convention says one line when a fold joins \"the same two plates\", but here the tab and the flange are separate panels in the CAD.\n  - Merging also conflicts with the contract: each measured bend position must have its own line, so a merge would mean dropping the tab's measured position to UNKNOWN.\n- **The recipe-excluded fold (28870000 FULL)** has no recipe bend to report it on. The one crease the engine does flag on that scan is 33 mm away, so it is a different feature.\n- **The rolled 28870000 SCAN_1** still reads WRONG_PART_SUSPECTED. Relaxing that test would risk the synthetic tier's never-pass rule for wrong or mirrored parts.\n- **Known limitation:** a part with every bend folded the wrong way and a nearly symmetric datum still reads as the good part turned over. The single-bend 44211000 probe shows this, with every characteristic PASS, as iteration 5's engine also reads it.\n\n**Ledger check is failing for a reason outside the engine.** Another workflow edited `contracts/production/inspection_result.py` at 01:44 (contracts fingerprint `5f7e6a8c\u2026` \u2192 `78e31787\u2026`). Every scorecard now reports `CONTRACTS_CODE_CHANGED_SINCE_FREEZE`, and the synthetic tier adds `FREEZE_LEDGER_MISMATCH`. I did not touch that file. The ledger check will keep failing until it is restored or re-frozen.\n\nEverything is in `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/a1/iter_6/`; open `CHANGE.md` first.\n- `engine.diff`\n- `validation/` (scorecards, diffs, probe logs)\n- `diag/`\n- `tools/`\n\nNew tests: `/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/tests/test_prod_engine_inspect_a1_iter6.py`"